(window.StoryDialogue = window.StoryDialogue || {})["ac-5"] = {"468245101":[["","\"Unfounded certainty is the privilege of fools.\""],["","Chapter 1"],["","XC 119, March — Outside an Abandoned ST Warehouse in West Milkhama"],["Melissa","Are you sure this is the right place?"],["Rebecca","According to word in the bounty hunter circles, that's right—this is the place Sámi put out for open recruitment."],["Melissa","Hmm..."],["","The depot in front of them exhibits a crude appearance, betraying the quality of its construction materials. Naturally, the surrounding land isn't paved with concrete or asphalt—it's nothing but raw earth."],["","Melissa glances down at her muddied shoes. It has been raining for the past two days, and the land around the depot has become a thick quagmire."],["","They walk with effort, leaving deep footprints in the viscous soil."],["Melissa","It's a bit strange... If this really is their base, then why are there no traces of STs coming and going?"],["Rebecca","Could be no one comes around here. Sámi's pay's so thin even a greenhorn like me wouldn't saddle up for it."],["Melissa","Even if no other bounty hunters came through, their STs would have left some traces. I doubt they'd be meticulous enough to erase everything."],["","Melissa is right. Even Light STs leave clearly visible tracks on terrain like this. In many cities, roads are subject to strict regulations limiting the load STs can place on them."],["Rebecca","The way you say it makes it sound like a trap... Better pull back and prepare some more."],["Melissa","No more delays! This has to be settled today!"],["Rebecca","Alright. But don't forget, every time you get all worked up and make a mess—I'm the one who has to clean it up."],["","Melissa switches off her brain, stomps forward aggressively, and bangs on the small metal door beside the depot's main entrance. Rebecca shrugs and follows."],["","The piercing clang echoes through the depot, ensuring anyone inside will hear it. After a short while, Melissa hears footsteps approaching."],["","A simple-looking young man opens the door."],["???","Hello? Who's there...?"],["Rebecca","This guy looks so honest, like he's easy to bully..."],["Melissa","I'm Melissa, a senior bounty hunter, and the one behind me is Rebecca, a top-tier hunter. We saw your job posting online."],["???","Uh... that job posting? I didn't think anyone would bite at that rate."],["Melissa","You're paying far too little! It's exploitative! That's the rate from, what, ten years ago!?"],["Rebecca","Correction, even ten years ago it wasn't this low."],["Hayato","We said the same to Sámi—\"If you don't offer more money, no one will come...\" Oh, I forgot to introduce myself, I'm Hayato."],["","After the unusual introduction, Hayato opens the door, and invites the two inside."],["Hayato","Come in, I'll help you get in touch with Sámi... May I ask, if the rate is so low, why did you apply?"],["Melissa","Apply for the job?"],["","Rebecca behind her can't hold back and lets out a little giggle, while an exasperated Melissa begins to explain the real reason for their call."],["Melissa","Ahem... Well, Sámi once had a twenty-year ST loan with Laniakea, an ST manufacturer under the UNCS. He's been in default for a year. According to the terms of the loan contract and local laws, we..."],["Rebecca","To put it simply, kid, we're here to collect the debt!"],["","Let's turn back the clock a bit..."],["","When did this girl, once tormented by debt, find herself in the service of those who hold the purse strings?"],["","XC 119, February — Rayneburg"],["","At 6 pm yesterday, fierce combat erupted in the Parill Desert buffer zone, leaving the UNCS Acting Viceroy Arnold Whiteread MIA."],["","At 9 pm, Vesper hijacked television broadcasts island-wide, taking credit for both the Milthus strike and Viceroy Arnold's vanishing act. They announced their demands..."],["Rebecca","Things seem real busy over in the east lately."],["","The two are on their way back home from the Doll Group office. Rebecca is driving, while Melissa, feeling bored, fiddles with the radio. Eventually she finds a bit of serious content amidst the noise of ads and gossip."],["","Although civilian comms devices cannot reach the east of the island, bounty hunters and their upgraded models are still able to get through. As reported by the DL News Agency, East Milkhama is in complete upheaval."],["Melissa","Sounds quite serious..."],["","Being in West Milkhama, it's difficult for them to imagine the scenes of horror occurring in the east. With a new governor, Rayneburg has entered a period of prosperity."],["","It's the weekend now. The traffic slows to a crawl as everyone takes to their cars."],["","Melissa rolls up the car window, shutting out the suffocating noise of the city, and focuses on the news report."],["Melissa","It seems this [Madam] they appointed is pretty capable. Things were a mess a few months ago, but once she arrived, our work basically disappeared."],["Rebecca","True, true... Hey... should we take a trip east?"],["Melissa","What for?"],["Rebecca","You said it yourself, things have been too peaceful in the west lately. No contracts, no bounties, nothing."],["Rebecca","You've got another interest payment to Alyson coming up, haven't you? I don't mind if you use the rent to cover it. I mean, I used to live in my ST, after all..."],["Melissa","But Alyson also warned us that if we head to East Milkhama, she won't be able to cover for us anymore."],["Rebecca","That's right... Melissa, is it just me, or have you been acting a bit off lately?"],["Melissa","Me? No... Have I?"],["Rebecca","Ever since I mentioned the debt, you've been acting strange, like you're holding back a smile."],["Melissa","Huh? Really?"],["","Melissa's pursed lips, clenched teeth and puffed cheeks barely manage to stifle a grin."],["Rebecca","And since when do you listen to Alyson? Usually it's me quoting Alyson to persuade you, not the other way round."],["Melissa","Actually, I don't think Alyson is all that bad. I think we just misunderstood her before..."],["Rebecca","Enough, already! Just say what you want to say. Come on—what's on your mind?"],["Melissa","Oh, fine. I can't say no to you. I'll tell you..."],["Melissa","We've completely paid off our debt to Alyson!"],["","Melissa raises her arms and cheers. Rebecca glances over, sighs, and offers a small smile as she eases the car forward."],["Rebecca","First of all, that's your debt, not mine. Secondly, I remember there should be... around two million more to go, right?"],["Melissa","That's right, but half a year ago, Alyson recommended a few of Doll's financial products to me. I randomly chose one, and somehow the returns started skyrocketing within a few months."],["Rebecca","Oh? How much did you make?"],["Melissa","Well, I only invested around forty thousand, and it went up to almost fifty thousand! That's a net return of 25%!"],["Rebecca","That's not quite two million though, is it..."],["Melissa","Yeah, I was really anxious at the time. Alyson kept talking about opportunities, about how, if I missed them, I'd never be able to pay off my interest, let alone the debt..."],["Rebecca","So..."],["Melissa","She said that in light of my hard work, she had decided to lend me some money to purchase the latest Doll Group private equity securities..."],["Rebecca","What!?"],["","A red light lights up in the distance, causing the vehicle in front to suddenly stop. Rebecca slams on the brakes, and the two inside jolt against their seatbelts."],["","Rebecca puts her cowboy hat back on and looks at Melissa with a forced calmness."],["","No smoking in the car... Chewing gum? A toothpick? She wishes for anything that can calm her frayed nerves."],["Rebecca","How much did you borrow from her?"],["Melissa","Something like three million... Why are you so worked up? As long as we earn it back and repay it..."],["Rebecca","Do you even know what you bought?"],["Melissa","Of course I know! You don't think I'm the kind of person who gets talked into a mountain of debt without understanding a single thing, do you?"],["Melissa","After all, I made nearly half the principal back on my first investment, so my judgment isn't that bad..."],["Rebecca","Alright, just tell me what you bought."],["","The car behind blares its horn, reminding Rebecca to close the gap in front. She clicks her tongue, rolls down the window, and flips the driver off. Her anger sated, she pulls over to the side of the road."],["","Home can wait. Right now, there are more important things to worry about. Like the car getting repossessed..."],["Melissa","Let me think, she probably said something like this back then..."],["Alyson","The security we are about to launch is backed by ST mortgages, currently the most popular and profitable type on Milkhama Island... Oh, by the way, the ones I previously asked you to choose were all of this type, you just didn't realize it."],["Alyson","To put it simply, it's an investment product backed by ST mortgage loans. Most of these loans come from banks and financial institutions, who then package them into a mortgage pool, and then..."],["Alyson","Let me put it in simpler terms. Those finance guys just love to make it sound complicated. They like to make you feel like only they can do it. I don't like that."],["Alyson","Take Rebecca for example. She bought her Boyer not long after arriving in West Milkhama. She was only 18 years old at the time. Do you really think she could afford the cost of that entire ST?"],["Alyson","Even the current mass produced models cost three to four hundred thousand dollars, which is still beyond what a bounty hunter just getting started can afford. So she accepted a loan agreement from Laniakea, funded by some bank within the UNCS, to purchase it."],["Alyson","Due to policy support, the floating interest rate for purchasing STs was initially very low, which was equivalent to Rebecca borrowing money without paying interest, allowing her to make installment payments for the ST without any pressure."],["Alyson","So, a kind of mortgage was created, essentially an IOU. Whoever holds this IOU is the one Rebecca needs to repay."],["Alyson","Not only individuals, but also organizations and armies—every day on Milkhama, thousands of ST loans are established, with countless funds flowing into the bond market, becoming chips for people to trade."],["Alyson","You don't need to know about interest rate cuts, dynamic interest rate changes, monetary policy... these are more complex topics. In short, as a bounty hunter running around all day, you definitely understand the importance of STs better than I do."],["Alyson","Death is the best salesman. To survive and win in battle, people will keep buying STs, and to become stronger, they will continue to upgrade and replace them. This market keeps expanding and never ends."],["Alyson","In this era, the best collateral bonds are supported by ST loans. In time, we who hold these bonds will naturally make an absolute fortune."],["Alyson","By then, Melissa, your debts will be written off."],["Rebecca","Melissa, the next time you're thinking of buying some strange IOUs from Alyson, you should discuss it with me first."],["Melissa","Didn't I show you the expected returns when I came? Not only can we pay off the debt, but we can even earn an extra million or so..."],["Rebecca","I just don't trust money that isn't earned with my own two hands. And borrowing from Alyson just to buy in? Hell... sometimes I think signing up to be experimented on by Obsidian might've been the smarter play."],["Melissa","That's why I didn't want to tell you—because I knew you'd lecture me like this!"],["","The two of them follow Hayato through the ST depot, engaging in their routine bickering along the way."],["","The two of them closely observe their surroundings. This place isn't the cavernous warehouse they expected. On the contrary, although the air is filled with the smell of dust, most of the platforms are occupied by STs."],["","Most of them are cheap, old models like Lanius and Tiktaalik. They are covered with rust from being kept in storage so long, but most are intact. With a little care, they would perform just fine."],["Melissa","Hayato, are these STs all yours?"],["Hayato","Hmm... I think Sámi only rents the depot. These STs were probably left behind by the previous mercs."],["Melissa","And they just left them here...?"],["Hayato","I don't really get it either... According to Sunny, sometimes it's better to buy a new model than repair an old one. The monthly payments aren't much anyway."],["Rebecca","Even if you fix them up and sell them second-hand, there are basically no mercenaries who would buy them, right?"],["Hayato","Yeah, everyone would definitely switch to better models, which would allow them to complete higher-level jobs and earn bigger bounties... Besides, the labor cost for machinists and the parts for STs are really expensive. Few mercenaries can afford it."],["Rebecca","Even taking them to the recycling plant costs money, right? And with that time, it makes more sense to just do more missions and get a better ST."],["Hayato","Yeah, Sunny complained about that too. You know quite a bit, Rebecca."],["Rebecca","Of course, I've been in the bounty hunting business for a few years now. There's a lot of overlap with mercenary work. It's all common knowledge."],["Melissa","..."],["","Melissa can't really join the conversation. She isn't that familiar with the market, as her ST, replacements, and modification parts were all provided by her father."],["","After assisting Alyson, any ST-related requirements were compiled by her into a list, then procured by Doll's personnel. Rebecca was visibly taken aback by the subsidy at the time, reacting as if she had been handed an unbelievable windfall."],["","She knows almost everything about STs and is one of the best machinists around. But the only thing she doesn't understand is the market that lies behind them."],["","Now it seems that this ignorance might be her undoing."],["Melissa","Something's wrong..."],["","A vague sense of unease begins creeping up on Melissa."],["","She cannot articulate it. What is this feeling?"],["Hayato","Please wait here, I'll go get Sámi."],["","Walking to the other end of the depot, Hayato greets someone and then enters a small room opposite the main door."],["","Melissa and her companion wait patiently for nearly a minute. Suddenly, there is movement. They hear the muffled sound of an ST outside. They've been had."],["","Words were unnecessary. They exchange a brief glance and bolt back in the direction of their STs."],["","Seconds later, the depot's main gate is blown open by an ST's rocket launcher. On the other side lies a large bridge, where numerous guards lie in wait."],["","Looks like trouble has arrived."]],"468245301":[["","It takes some work, but once they subdue Hayato's ST, the mercenaries besieging them begin to retreat, disappearing from sight shortly thereafter."],["","This wasn't a fight to the death, just business. And all sides understood this."],["Hayato","If only we had better STs, we'd definitely..."],["Rebecca","Judging by your appearance, you must be from the NDF, right? So why are you making excuses like a merc?"],["","As the frustrated Hayato vainly tries to move his disabled ST, Melissa and Rebecca climb atop his cockpit. Rebecca's rifle aims through the damaged cabin, straight at his head."],["Rebecca","Stop right there. Maybe you should get the thing moving again before worrying about how good it is."],["Melissa","ST performance isn't everything... but why did you attack us, anyway? Sámi's orders?"],["Hayato","...He said that if any Laniakea debt collectors come knocking, we should deal with them here."],["Melissa","But we're not from Laniakea. His ST loan bonds were bought by the Doll Fund, and I was sent over to investigate..."],["Rebecca","You're wasting your breath. We're just here to collect."],["Rebecca","And according to Alyson, you'll only be allowed to liquidate your securities once Sámi, the super debtor, has been dealt with."],["Melissa","That's right... So Hayato, you've already been defeated. Just tell us Sámi's whereabouts... This has nothing to do with you."],["Hayato","But if I do that, Sámi won't pay me, and if that happens..."],["Rebecca","Think it through. Sámi is in major debt. Do you really expect someone like him to pay you?"],["Hayato","Before you came, he paid us on time."],["Hayato","He even buys us personal insurance, ST insurance—all that kind of stuff. We get two days off a week, and he provides free ST maintenance and upgrades... If you nab him, won't I lose my job?"],["Rebecca","...Seriously, is the treatment for retired mercenaries really that good?"],["Hayato","I still need to support my younger sister, and I have to cover her college expenses..."],["Rebecca","Cry me a river. Melissa, don't let him sway you..."],["Melissa","It seems Sámi has enough spare cash to throw around, so he should be able to gather up enough to cover the interest, right?"],["Rebecca","...When did you become so cold-blooded, missy?"],["Melissa","When I thought about the possibility of our debt doubling..."],["Sunny","Hey! Hey, hey, Hayato, I must've missed your distress signal earlier when I was on the john. What's the situation now?"],["Hayato","Shhh, Sunny, now's not a good time..."],["Melissa","Oh? Is that your friend?"],["","Rebecca raises her gun. Hayato has no choice but to close his mouth, sitting stiffly and not daring to move."],["","Melissa crouches down, fumbles around a while, and finds the maintenance switch on the side of the cockpit. She opens the hatch with ease and grabs the communicator next to Hayato."],["Melissa","Are you one of Sámi's people, too?"],["Sunny","...Oh, guess you already got to Hayato, huh?"],["Sunny","Is it that GKD Parcel Service again...? No, I don't remember them having a girl who sounds like she's barely old enough to drive."],["Melissa","Actually, I'm an adult, and... Forget it, you don't seem too surprised Hayato was defeated."],["Sunny","With skills like his, of course not. We mainly recruited him because he looks honest and wouldn't easily arouse suspicion."],["Melissa","But he's still one of you, right? If you don't want him to get hurt, tell me where Sámi is."],["Sunny","Is that a threat? Hard to tell with a voice like yours."],["Melissa","...Rebecca, your turn."],["Rebecca","Okay!"],["","Melissa tosses the communicator to Rebecca. She catches it, tilts her head, and holds it between her shoulder and ear. The gun in her hand remains aimed at Hayato's forehead, unwavering."],["","Rebecca talks with him in a low voice for a while, then hands the communicator back to Melissa."],["Sunny","*sigh* Okay... First, I need to know if you're with the UNCS. If you are, then you can mess Hayato up until he's unrecognisable. I don't care. I still won't say a word."],["Melissa","Rest assured. We're with the Doll Group and have nothing to do with the UNCS."],["Sunny","Alright, I'll send you an address for the port. When the time comes, we'll exchange the hostage for the... information."],["Melissa","We'll be there soon."],["","After confirming the location, Melissa hangs up the communicator and nods to Rebecca, who then puts down her gun."],["","She extends her hand to the bewildered Hayato inside the cabin."],["Melissa","Hey, stop lying around in there, we're in a hurry."],["Hayato","Wha... what? I thought you'd knock me out, and..."],["Rebecca","Come on, on your feet? Do we have to carry you?"],["Melissa","It like I said: our goal is to find Sámi. We're not interested in any unnecessary violence. We don't get paid for that."],["","Seeing Hayato's hesitation, Melissa takes the initiative to step forward and bends down to pull him up."],["Melissa","Besides, if you really care about your family, maybe you should consider a less... questionable career path."],["Melissa","Even if you earn a little less, that's okay. Don't try shouldering everything yourself. Be honest with your family—that's more important than anything else."],["Melissa","They'll understand."],["","The Ashes Base"],["Chloe","Marcus, we've found the whereabouts of that Sunny."],["Marcus","...Who?"],["","Chloe steps into the command room to report, only to be met with a voice muffled by mountains of documents."],["Chloe","He was from the Black Hawk Squad—they previously served the UNCS. They were defeated by the GKD, leading their captain, Crotti, to resign in disgrace."],["Marcus","I remember now, that Crotti secretly recruited mercenaries to launch a terrorist attack within DL territory. Due to joint liability, all former Black Hawk Squad members were dismissed."],["Chloe","That's right, some of them became mercenaries, and even more followed that Sámi into a lot of gray market businesses..."],["Marcus","Sámi again... Oh, oh, it's this guy, right?"],["","A report is precisely pulled out from the files. It's clear she knows these documents well."],["Marcus","He used to be in Laniakea's security forces, but was dismissed after causing civilian casualties during a mission. He then formed his own mercenary group and began operating externally. Recently, he participated in a raid on a Laniakea warehouse and is now a wanted man..."],["Chloe","Hmm, this is a warrant recently issued by the UNCS throughout all West Milkhama. We might be able to get some clues from Sunny. I'll take some people there right now..."],["Marcus","Wait... Wait a minute, let me take care of this."],["","Marcus's head suddenly pops out from the documents. His outburst sounds more like a plea for help than a request."],["Chloe","Have you completed the inventory, the personnel reorganization, the NDF cooperation documents....?"],["Marcus","Stop... just... please, I beg you."],["","The temporary leader clasps his hands together and pleads with Chloe. Faced with this pathetic sight, Chloe can only sigh helplessly."],["Chloe","And... at least when it comes to logistics and manpower..."],["Marcus","Done. All done. The government supplies have been distributed, and everyone's received their share. There's absolutely nothing missing!"],["Marcus","As for the detailed cooperation plan with the NDF, Ana's still arranging it. The remaining loose ends, well, they can wait..."],["Chloe","You're just fishing for an excuse to slack off, right?"],["Marcus","What are you talking about? I just want to give our guys more time to rest. Don't worry, I'll take care of it. I am the Ashes' temporary leader, after all!"],["Chloe","I know..."],["","Marcus's unusually high energy does not infect Chloe. Although she has improved a lot over the past few months, her face still carries an unmistakable melancholy."],["","But it cannot be helped. Ever since that man disappeared, reappeared, and finally vanished again in betrayal, things have never been the same among the Ashes."],["","For them, their battle is far from done."],["Marcus","Chloe, we've been through so many things in the past that we never wanted to accept, yet couldn't change."],["","Chloe turns to leave. Marcus stands and calls out."],["Marcus","All we can do for now is keep moving forward. Sooner or later, we'll encounter that bastard again."],["Marcus","And for when that moment comes, we've got to be ready."],["Chloe","But... But I always feel..."],["","Chloe doesn't turn around, but her voice sounds choked."],["Chloe","Even after he did those things... did he really betray us...? I just... don't know anymore..."],["Marcus","That's why we have to find him."],["","Marcus steps forward, placing his hand on Chloe's shoulder, as they both gaze outside the command room at the bustling and lively scene in the Ashes base."],["","This was a hope that didn't come easily—and this time, he will protect it at all costs."],["Marcus","When the time comes, he'll explain to us exactly what's going on."]],"468248101":[["","Chapter 2"],["","Doll Mech Factory"],["Melissa","That's the current situation. We're trying to get Sunny to give us some intel on Sámi."],["Alyson","I see. Looking forward to the next update."],["","After hanging up, Alyson gazes at the Doll Industries production line through her office window."],["","Piles of documents and reports are stacked on the desk behind her. Since her troops were withdrawn and her actions restricted, she has begun an investigation she'd always had at the back of her mind."],["","The various incidents in East Milkhama have temporarily been handed over to Fia and the others. As for West Milkhama, the only ones available are Melissa and one other... but that should be enough."],["","Although to the outside world, Miss Alyson seems to just throw cash at her problems, she can also work magic on a shoestring."],["","Through the information brought back by Melissa, the cards in her hand are already sufficient."],["","From now on, Alyson will give it everything she's got."],["Alyson","Hey, how's the ST credit index at the moment?"],["Analyst","Miss, the index has fallen by around one point over the last two months."],["Alyson","How much time left before it becomes junk?"],["Analyst","Junk? Well... according to a recent ST sales forum, the recent uptick in default rates suggests the bubble will remain regional, mainly due to the collapse of Blair in West Milkhama..."],["Alyson","Those morons..."],["","Without saying another word, Alyson turns around and walks up to the computer. She pushes the analyst aside and begins operating swiftly."],["","As anticipated, the index for ST-backed collateralized debt obligations continues to surge. It's not just corporations like Doll looking for gains—countless investors, including Melissa, are hooked as well."],["","The bubble keeps expanding, sweeping everyone higher with it."],["Alyson","I said we should quit while we're ahead. Why doesn't anyone else get it?"],["Analyst","Miss, the market is still very healthy, your worries are..."],["Alyson","You know what? Just a few months ago, I saw the sales pitch for Doll securities, and I read it verbatim to some naive chick. She took it hook, line, and sinker."],["Alyson","To be frank, you pros aren't too different from her. Before the panic, you're blind to the real risks."],["Analyst","What do you mean? These bonds are backed by thousands of ST loans..."],["Alyson","I've read them all."],["Analyst","...Huh? I thought only the lawyers..."],["Alyson","I'm starting to doubt they know exactly what they've created..."],["Alyson","A bunch of white-collar guys who've never set foot inside an ST, just watching the market go up and up. Building this ST market piece by piece, stacking loan upon loan like they're building blocks..."],["Alyson","And who are the ones providing them with the building blocks?"],["Analyst","..."],["","The analyst remains silent. She doesn't understand how the young lady in front of her can question the value of this credit gold mine."],["","To a true believer like herself, Alyson's argument is as absurd as 2 + 2 = 5. It is as if she is saying black is white, up is down. She is at a loss."],["","In contrast, looking into the analyst's naive eyes, Alyson feels nauseated, but she has to continue."],["Alyson","The mercenaries were the first to bear the brunt, each taking out four, five loans for their STs. Then, they were followed by the ambitious ones, like Blair's troops, who also left mountains of bad debt."],["Alyson","Everyone thought they could make a fortune using STs, but few found real success. The scarier part was observing wave after wave of newcomers throwing themselves into the gamble, like lambs to the slaughter."],["Alyson","When the introductory interest rate period ends, mercenaries and speculators will be unable to refinance. The default rate will rocket, and the market will implode."],["Alyson","The invisible hand will give each of you a couple of slaps."],["","The higher you fly, the harder you fall."],["Alyson","Fundamentally, pushing the arms-trading business in this direction was unsound from the start, riddled with contradictions. What I find difficult is how no one seems to see it."],["Alyson","Get in touch with those old guys at HQ. It's time to talk to them about this."],["","Port Meeting Point"],["Rebecca","Heh... Hehehe... Hehe..."],["Melissa","Your laugh is so creepy... Are you really that excited?"],["Rebecca","Of course! This kind of hostage delivery scene is a classic trope in westerns. Usually, when the hostage is halfway, the cowboy's gun goes... pew, pew, pew!"],["","Rebecca excitedly demonstrates to Melissa to one side, using an imaginary revolver at her waist to take down a group of enemies across from her."],["Melissa","But isn't it usually the villains who threaten cowboys with hostages? Now we're the ones with the hostages..."],["Rebecca","What's the difference? Either way, the hostages run halfway before we start shooting. Does it matter which side they run from?"],["Rebecca","Don't sweat the small stuff, Melissa."],["Melissa","You're just looking for a fight, aren't you? Be careful, and try not to cause trouble if you can avoid it..."],["","Amidst their bickering, several STs have already arrived at the port. The two are approached by a group led by a portly gentleman."],["Sunny","You're Doll's people?"],["Melissa","That's right. Let's skip the pleasantries."],["","Melissa pushes Hayato forward, causing him to stumble toward Sunny. Rebecca raises her gun."],["","A shot hits the concrete by Hayato's feet, sending sparks and debris flying, making him yelp in surprise."],["Rebecca","Before he reaches your side—the info about Sámi. My gun's curious to know."],["Sunny","Whoa, whoa... Take it easy, cowgirl, I was just about to say..."],["","Faced with Rebecca's threat, Sunny simply laughs. His cheerful demeanor and quivering belly catch the attention of both."],["","Hayato turns his head, seemingly in fear of Rebecca's gun. But his eyes gaze right past her. Melissa senses something."],["","Turning around, her heart drops. An ST, perhaps lying in ambush since the beginning, peeks out from a container. Its machine gun is pointed right at them."],["Melissa","Rebecca, watch out!"],["","Bang!!!"],["","Melissa cries out and tackles Rebecca. As she pounces, her ST activates in response, knocking the ambusher aside as it begins to fire. The stray bullets of the misfired weapon leave a row of bullet holes in the container beside them."],["Melissa","You're kidding... You're actually using STs against humans?"],["Sunny","Tch... Autonomous AI? Looks like you've done quite a bit of preparation..."],["Marcus","Attention! This is the Ashes. Sunny and the others: Disarm immediately... Hm? Who are those two?"],["","The sound of whirring propellers approaches as a large fleet of ST transport aircraft flies overhead. New STs are airdropped, adding a third faction to the stand-off."],["","When one thinks they've made the perfect plan, complacency will surely lead to ruin."],["Rebecca","What's going on?! There are more?!"],["Melissa","Looks like UNCS... Whatever, we need to figure out how to protect ourselves first."]],"468248301":[["","On the wreckage-littered battlefield, only three units remain: Melissa, Marcus, and Sunny. A three-way stand-off ensues."],["Melissa","How did it end up like this again? I really didn't want any trouble!"],["Sunny","You really got me this time. I didn't expect you to team up with those strays from the Ashes..."],["Marcus","Strays? That's rich coming from a former Black Hawk Squad member."],["","Marcus takes a step forward, prompting the others to follow suit, each bringing their gun barrels closer in unison."],["Melissa","The Ashes... I remember you were supposed to be an organization formed by vets opposing the UNCS..."],["Marcus","We used to be, but now that Blair has fallen, we no longer have a reason to rebel."],["Melissa","No wonder you're all using UNCS equipment now. These things can't be cheap..."],["","Looking at Marcus and his squad's new gear, Melissa cannot resist making a comment. Having just recently learned the cost of outfitting a squad, she now feels a strong desire to show off her new knowledge."],["Marcus","Price? I didn't really think about it. Someone just said that if we get the job done well, everything's covered."],["Sunny","Hahaha... Hahahahaha!"],["Marcus","That's funny, is it?"],["Sunny","It seems you don't know what you've gotten yourselves into. This governor ain't as kind-hearted as Blair..."],["Melissa","Wait, hold on a second. From the sounds of it, you're holding on to some kind of major grudge and we were just caught up in it."],["Marcus","You're not here to make a trade? I heard Sunny is in charge of the local smuggling racket under Sámi's orders. I presumed there'd be some kind of double-cross going on here..."],["Melissa","We're from the Doll Group! Did we not just mention that?!"],["Marcus","..."],["","Only at times like this does Melissa feel grateful to be under Alyson's wing. Having a legitimate identity can save you a lot of trouble."],["","Marcus swings his shotgun away from Melissa and toward Sunny."],["","Now it's two against one."],["Sunny","Alright, alright, I surrender, I surrender. Happy now?"],["","Sunny's ST drops its gun and puts up its hands. Then the cockpit opens, and Sunny himself does the same."],["Melissa","Giving up so easily?"],["Sunny","So what? There's no need to fight to the death, right?"],["Marcus","A wise choice... So, if there's no problem, we'll take Sunny back for questioning, as a friend of Doll."],["Melissa","Wait, we have questions for him too. This time, he won't be able to pull anything funny."],["","Melissa points at Sunny with the ST's finger, threatening him as payback for the earlier ambush."],["Melissa","Tell me, where is Sámi hiding? Is he going to pay back the money or not?"],["Marcus","Wait, are you asking about... Sámi?"],["Melissa","Yes? And?"],["Marcus","We're after him too. It seems our goals are aligned."],["","Marcus's ST stands in front of Melissa, becoming a major roadblock between her and her mission."],["Marcus","Tell me, what are you after?"]],"468251101":[["","Chapter 3"],["","Doll Mech Factory"],["Alyson","Since when is it your place as a supervisor to address me?"],["Doll Supervisor","Miss, please remain calm. The directors are currently in a remote meeting with representatives from the UNCS..."],["","A holographic projection of the supervisor sits in front of Alyson, a nauseatingly fake smile on his face. Alyson's brow furrows with annoyance."],["","The best part of coming to Milkhama Island is not having to deal with these sorts..."],["Alyson","The UNCS people... That [Madam], right? What kind of deal's in the works?"],["Doll Supervisor","I'm sorry, that's strictly confidential. Even if I wanted to tell you, Miss, my clearance would still..."],["Alyson","I've reviewed the group's recent business operations. Looks like they secured priority lending rights for Laniakea's ST sales, right?"],["Alyson","Mercs and troops prefer the Doll Fund to the regular UNSC banks, which results in us holding ever more bad debt..."],["Alyson","And because we're the ones throwing around money, Laniakea's STs are flying off the shelves and into the hands of all sorts of groups. That [Madam] will definitely use this to curry favor..."],["Doll Supervisor","Sorry, whether your guess is correct or not, I can't disclose anything."],["Alyson","Then what's the point of even answering the phone?"],["","Even the seasoned negotiator finds his smile stiffening in the face of Alyson's rudeness."],["Doll Supervisor","Miss Alyson, ST collateral bonds are currently the most premium of premium assets on the market. I thought you understood that..."],["Alyson","Oh, be quiet! All you do is sit in an office staring at charts. You wanna lecture me about the markets? You're more worried about which club you'll crawl into after work."],["Alyson","That's all the market is—a mass of short-sighted fools like you, marching together in lockstep toward ruin!"],["Doll Supervisor","...It doesn't sound like you're entirely optimistic about the future of the ST market."],["Alyson","Oh, so you at least understand that much."],["Doll Supervisor","But the current ST market is indeed still in a growth phase. The collapse you anticipate could only happen if tens of thousands defaulted..."],["Alyson","That's true, everyone is eagerly awaiting new technology and new ST releases, which will lead more people into this trap."],["Doll Supervisor","Exactly, the Obsidian-related technology you submitted earlier proves this point."],["Alyson","They're wrong. All of them."],["Alyson","The signs of a bubble are unmistakable. The prices of new STs keep rising, and the only thing increasing is the number of ST loan scams..."],["Analyst","Miss Alyson, there's a call from Canary."],["Alyson","I'm busy right now. I'll call back later."],["","Suddenly interrupted, Alyson feels somewhat annoyed, but she quickly calms down. This is an opportunity to organize her thoughts..."],["","She understands the old guard at headquarters all too well. Their business is built on exploitation, and they are completely indifferent to the risks. How can it possibly last?"],["","It's a ridiculous situation. Never listening to reason, they only pay attention to the opinions they want to hear."],["","And they are right—she is a troublesome girl, always going against her elders."],["","But this was one of the main reasons she came to this island alone. Living in a place where everyone spoke past each other, where everyone blindly followed or believed. It was suffocating. She needed a place to breathe."],["","But now she'll hold her nose and confront those self-important people."],["","Not just for those elusive numbers, but for the reality those numbers represent."],["","After all, sometimes numbers can affect reality."],["Alyson","I'll say it again—let me talk to them."],["Doll Supervisor","Miss, I told you, they are having an important discussion with the UNCS representatives..."],["Alyson","Forget it, I have a backup number."],["","Without giving the supervisor any more chance to argue, Alyson cuts off the video communication, his smarmy smile disappearing in a flash."],["","She dials a number."],["","Those suits, gesturing in front of their charts and screens, will soon be rudely interrupted. Things are about to get awkward."],["","But why does she care so much? On the contrary, maybe it's just amusing..."],["","Thinking of this, a smile returns to Alyson's face."],["Melissa","...What should I do? Alyson actually hung up on me."],["Rebecca","How should I know?"],["","Rebecca shrugs with an indifferent expression, showing no empathy for Melissa, who is biting her nails between tightening screws."],["","The earlier commotion has come to an abrupt end. They are repairing the damage from the previous battle at a roadside ST repair shop."],["Melissa","But those Ashes don't listen to reason, do they? They outnumbered us and had the UNCS backing them, so they just drove us out."],["Rebecca","He also told you that after capturing Sámi, he would contact Doll's people to handle the debt issue, right?"],["Melissa","But Alyson told me to take anything anyone related to the UNCS says with a grain of salt..."],["Rebecca","Really? I feel like that Marcus seems pretty reliable. Looks like someone you could have a drink with."],["Melissa","..."],["","After tightening the last screw on Rebecca's ST, Melissa stands up, glaring at Rebecca with a hint of annoyance."],["Melissa","What's been going on with you these days? Everything I say, you contradict."],["Rebecca","Right."],["Melissa","What?!"],["","This time, she agrees, quickly and without fuss."],["Rebecca","Ever since you got it into your head to get rich overnight, you've been acting so weird... Melissa, what were you thinking betting your future on something you don't even understand?!"],["Melissa","I... I do understand! Anyone can see the trends in the ST market..."],["Rebecca","Before this, you didn't even know how much an ST cost, did you?"],["Melissa","..."],["","She's speechless..."],["Melissa","It's clearly not my fault... Sámi defaulting on his debt caused a domino effect! The securities got frozen and... once it's clarified..."],["Rebecca","But actually, Sámi has always had a bad reputation, right? With a little research, anyone could have guessed that someone like Sámi wouldn't repay."],["Rebecca","But basic research, that was bit too much, wasn't it?"],["Melissa","Did you see that document? It was literally thicker than my forearm."],["","The more she tries to explain, the worse it sounds..."],["Rebecca","Even if I don't understand those indices or markets you're talking about... I think there are some things that only someone like me, who's been on the front lines for years, can understand."],["Melissa","..."],["Rebecca","Recently, more and more mercenaries, driven by temporary success, have been using their rewards to upgrade to more advanced STs in hopes of completing higher-level missions."],["Rebecca","This is only natural—everyone strives for bigger and better things. Or perhaps, everyone is afraid, as if stopping would allow something behind them to catch up."],["Rebecca","Especially in Milkhama, with its booming economy, a land of opportunity..."],["","Rebecca doesn't look at Melissa. She just sits on her ST's shoulder, observing the desert beyond the workshop. Staring, silently, as if observing the whole island."],["Rebecca","Some mercenaries might realize something's amiss, but there's no choice. When you find your opponents have upgraded to better equipment, what choice do you have?"],["Rebecca","And what you're investing in is the future of these people. That's something to look forward to, is it?"],["Rebecca","Those mercenaries, those bounty hunters. For them, there's no future. They live in the now."],["Melissa","..."],["Rebecca","So Melissa, what are you planning to do now?"],["Melissa","..."],["","Standing next to Rebecca, Melissa shifts from initial anger to silence. Her two hands, once clenched into fists, now hang limply at her sides."],["","She knows it is pointless to keep arguing."],["Melissa","Look, I know. I know, okay? ...*sigh*... What if I ran back to Alyson and begged her to forgive the loan and pretend nothing ever happened...?"],["Rebecca","You know that, to her, it's not about the money."],["Melissa","This isn't me turning a blind eye to my own mistakes. All I can do now is do my best now to make up for everything."],["Rebecca","So this mission isn't over yet..."],["Melissa","Um... Rebecca? I'm sorry, okay? If anything like this comes up in the future, I promise to discuss it with you first."],["","Melissa apologizes to Rebecca sincerely, her eyes slightly red. Rebecca's lecture seems to have been effective."],["Melissa","I keep getting us in trouble... But for now, we need to follow those Ashes. They might lead us to Sámi."],["Marcus","So, is this where Sámi's been hiding?"],["","Leading an Ashes detachment, Marcus pilots his ST into a dilapidated factory. From the marks left on the ground, it seems another unit has just left."],["Marcus","The NDF's detector didn't find any trace of the stolen goods. It seems they were moved a while ago."],["Ashes Soldier","Boss, be careful!"],["","Bang!!!"],["","A pile bunker jolts forward from the back of the room. A soldier leaps to protect Marcus, but Marcus skillfully parries the attack."],["","The two pile bunkers collide with a crash. The two STs each take a step back, sizing each other up."],["Keller","You saw it coming, huh? To think you'd withstand such a strike..."],["Marcus","Nice hit, but I know quite a few characters who are handy with a pile bunker. As for you... you'd better quit while you can."],["Keller","Enough talk. Until we confirm Sámi has left West Milkhama, you won't be leaving here."]],"468251301":[["Marcus","Keller, I've seen your intel too. You were among the first batch of mercenaries to follow Sámi... But didn't you all scatter after being crushed by the GKD Parcel Service?"],["Keller","Hmph... What's it to you?"],["","Keller's ST, reduced to just the body, still doesn't fall. For mercenaries, they're tough—but still no match for Marcus's squad."],["","These warriors of the Ashes, risen from the fires of war, are nothing less than elite."],["Marcus","Now that West Milkhama has finally settled down, isn't it time you go separate ways? There's no need to follow that lunatic Sámi, is there?"],["Keller","You make it sound so easy. If the world were really as simple as you say, then why'd you become the NDF's lackeys?"],["Marcus","Hmm... That's different..."],["","Marcus wants to argue. This anger he feels... Is there truth in Keller's words?"],["","When it comes down to it, why do the Ashes still exist? They were originally an organization to stop that warmonger, Blair. What purpose do they have left?"],["","As leader, this is a question that can only be answered by Marcus."],["Keller","Haha! Cat got your tongue? Then let me tell you."],["Keller","Besides fighting, there's nothing else for guys like you. It's all you've ever known."],["Marcus","Nonsense. Now we're fighting for the peace of Milkhama. And if it wasn't for troublemakers like you disturbing that peace..."],["","There's no need for Keller to refute it. Even Marcus feels the weakness of his words."],["","Maintaining peace is an NDF duty. Those who left did so to fight for NDF reform."],["","Now that this has been accomplished, why don't they return to the NDF? Maybe it's because they're still carrying wartime baggage that's difficult to reconcile..."],["","No, the [Madam] already offered amnesty, but most of the Ashes still chose not to join."],["","Perhaps they still distrust the NDF. But if that's the case, why are they still accepting aid from the NDF and actively carrying out missions on their behalf?"],["Keller","It seems I overestimated you all. A bunch of saps who don't even know what they want. You're hired government thugs. Even I could do that..."],["Keller","We've resorted to all means for survival. I'd definitely prefer working for the NDF over that lunatic Sámi... but we don't have a choice, do we?"],["Marcus","Enough of your babbling."],["Marcus","No matter what, you can't wash away the damage you've done by assisting Sámi. The law will punish you accordingly..."],["Ashes Soldier","Captain, we've tracked Sámi's whereabouts based on the ST's trail..."],["Marcus","Great, send the coordinates over right away. I'm heading there now."],["Keller","It's useless. After all this time, Sámi must have already..."],["Ashes Soldier","When we tracked the target, he was about to board the mineral train to escape. Our chance was slipping away."],["Ashes Soldier","But those two Doll Group mercenaries managed to intercept and pin him down. Proceed to the coordinates immediately to support!"]],"468254101":[["","Chapter Four"],["Melissa","Sámi, stop!"],["Sámi","That's not an NDF ST... You're not from Laniakea, are you?"],["","Just like in a classic western, Melissa and Rebecca face off against Sámi, with nothing between them but yellow sand drifting in the wind."],["Rebecca","By the way, I actually have some tumbleweeds behind my ST. Should I bring them out to add some atmosphere?"],["Melissa","Shh, leave this to me... Sámi, calm down first. We're from the Doll Group..."],["Sámi","The Doll Group? What's going on? I have no beef with you."],["Sámi","Enough. The train will arrive soon. Whatever it is, wait until I get to the other side and then we'll talk about it..."],["","Sámi's emotions appeared mirrored in his ST. He anxiously watches the tracks, hoping for the train to appear."],["","His anxiety is reflected in the setup he'd prepared—barriers, and gunports with their sights set on visitors. Had they been NDF STs, he would've skipped the pleasantries."],["Melissa","Long story short, your debt with Laniakea has been transferred to the Doll Group..."],["Melissa","And, basically, part of it belongs to me."],["Sámi","You mean they sold my IOU to you, so now it's your turn to collect the debt?"],["Melissa","That's one way to understand it... In any case, Sámi, you took out a substantial ST loan, enough to arm an entire unit, which has been overdue for more than a year now."],["Melissa","We demand an explanation. Even if you're currently unable to repay, we can provide a suitable restructuring plan. An interest rate reduction for a suitable period is also..."],["","Melissa racks her brain to repeat the finance-speak Alyson taught her."],["Sámi","Enough. I don't want to hear any more of your corporate nonsense!"],["Sámi","Here's the deal. What we were told is that the documents were a formality—that as long as we got jobs done, they'd equip me and my crew with the best STs."],["Sámi","But those bastards were in bed with the NDF from the start! One mistake, and they throw me in the slammer. When I get out, I'm barred from taking contracts through the company and left carrying this debt—barely scraping by on Milkhama..."],["Rebecca","...So they dangled high-paying company jobs and got you to sign an enormous loan?"],["Rebecca","When you put it that way, Alyson comes off pretty decent. She doesn't even make us provide our own STs. I guess that counts for something..."],["Melissa","Sorry, but at the end of the day, it was you who signed the agreement."],["Melissa","You clearly wanted better STs and higher profits, yet you're unwilling to take on the corresponding risks and responsibilities. People like you are pathetic."],["Sámi","You're just a corporate lackey. Don't pretend you understand."],["Melissa","*sigh* I do understand, all too well. I also owe money to the Doll Group..."],["","The surprise leaves Sámi momentarily speechless."],["Melissa","But I'm not running like you. I'm working to pay off the debt I racked up through my own stupidity. Then maybe I'll have a chance to start over."],["Melissa","I was dumb and immature. Buying bad debts, trying to get rich overnight. And now I'm here bickering with you. But despite all this, I don't regret it. I'll take responsibility for it. I got myself here, and I'll get myself out."],["Rebecca","Uh, you sure seemed like you were regretting it a lot earlier, dollface..."],["Melissa","So, Sámi, don't even think about escaping. Get off that ST right now and explain to me how you plan to repay this debt! Fulfill your responsibility like a man!"],["Melissa","After this, whether you get caught by the UNCS or whatever, it's nothing to do with me! I'll sell off my securities—I might lose some money, but that's fine..."],["Sámi","..."],["Sámi","It seems like your brain has really been messed up by the company to say something like that..."],["Melissa","Right, you're so anti-corporate. That's why you were offering wages lower than the rates TEN years ago!"],["Sámi","I'm quite generous to those willing to stick by my side, it's just that the current situation is... well, even at that price, as long as my recruits accept it... no harm, no foul, right?"],["Rebecca","Ugh, this guy is such a hypocrite."],["Rebecca","Melissa, why don't we just get straight to it? The final showdown in a western doesn't usually have this much chit-chat..."],["Melissa","You're right, why am I wasting my time? Rebecca, let's go!"],["Melissa","Remember, don't damage the equipment on site! I'll have to collect it later to help him pay off his debt!"]],"468254301":[["Marcus","...What happened?"],["","He expects a brutal fight to be waiting for him—but when he reaches the coordinates, all that greets him is wreckage strewn across the ground..."],["","No—most of the facilities and STs aren't destroyed at all. They've been shut down through precise, deliberate means."],["","The two Doll mercenaries cautiously protect the scene to prevent further destruction, as instructed by the NDF, ensuring that the batch of Laniakea supplies hijacked by Sámi is not damaged."],["","Marcus understands that, were it him, the scene probably couldn't have been maintained so perfectly."],["Melissa","Oh? Is it that Ashes guy?"],["","Melissa, who is counting supplies on the ground, notices Marcus's arrival. She hops around to catch Marcus's attention and then points to the side."],["","Sámi and his accomplices are tied up together. Rebecca, who stands guard nearby, throws a smile at Marcus."],["Marcus","The two of you took care of all of them?"],["","Marcus dismounts from his ST and walks toward Melissa, still in disbelief as he looks around the scene."],["Melissa","We had to use a few tricks, but essentially... yeah, we took care of them."],["Melissa","And you're looking for Sámi, right? He's over there, so consider this my apology for following you without permission."],["Marcus","Thanks for that... but what are you planning to do now?"],["Melissa","According to instructions from above, I'm preparing to take all the facilities and STs here to help Sámi pay off his debts. After recovery, they should cover his dues for a few years."],["","Melissa smiles brightly. A wonderful new life awaits her—how could she not look forward to it?"],["Marcus","Uh, that might be a problem. We've also received instructions to recover all facilities and STs related to Sámi..."],["Melissa","Wait, all of this equipment was secured with defaulted loans. I have the legal documents to support this. You should report to your superiors. There's probably a misunderstanding."],["Melissa","If you end up reclaiming them and then have to send them back to me, wouldn't that be quite troublesome?"],["Marcus","No rush for now—just wait a moment..."],["","After reporting the situation, Marcus leans against his ST and waits, while Melissa continues humming and bouncing around, inspecting her spoils."],["","In the past, he would have prioritized the mission above all else, but Melissa's openness and smile makes him think twice."],["","Before long, the latest instructions are relayed."],["Marcus","Uh... Melissa, right? This is the person sent by the higher-ups. I heard they just spoke with Doll. They'll explain the current situation to you."],["Machinist","Hello, are you Melissa, the mercenary dispatched by the Doll Group?"],["Melissa","Hello? Yeah, that's me. It should have been officially approved for us to recover the STs, right? I mean, as long as Alyson is involved, everything should be fine."],["Machinist","That's right, you can recover the parts of Sámi's original STs within an hour according to the previous agreement."],["Melissa","Now there's a time limit? Never mind, an hour is more than enough... Wait..."],["Melissa","What do you mean by \"original\"?"],["Machinist","Well, after the previous robbery, many parts of Sámi's STs were heavily modified, and those modified parts are assets of the UNCS."],["Machinist","If you claim these state assets during this commercial recovery, expect to be held legally accountable."],["Melissa","...Are you joking? Does Alyson know about this?"],["Machinist","This is the result of negotiations with the upper management of Doll."],["Melissa","This is ridiculous... Does that mean you're going to come after us over a single missing screw too?"],["Machinist","Logically speaking, yes."],["","Well, at least now she can empathize with Sámi..."],["","Melissa feels as though she is stuck in a paradox—licensed to cut flesh, but forbidden from drawing blood."],["Melissa","But why one hour? If it were a bit longer, maybe..."],["Machinist","Because this will interfere with the execution of other tasks assigned to the troops. Any delay and you will be held accountable for obstructing official duties."],["Melissa","..."],["","After a moment of silence, Melissa, with a tense expression, walks over to Rebecca."],["Rebecca","This time I can't speak up for you, so just be honest and... Huh? What are you doing?!"],["","Melissa suddenly snatches the rifle from Rebecca's hands and points it at Sámi's head."],["Melissa","Everyone, step aside! Don't move until we recover the STs!"],["Melissa","Sámi's life is in my hands now. If you want to take him back for credit, you'll have to deal with this gun first!"],["Rebecca","..."],["Marcus","..."],["Melissa","...Don't just stand there staring! Nothing to say? Okay..."],["Rebecca","Sorry, you guys keep an eye on her. I'll contact our superior—I reckon only she can handle this one."],["Marcus","Sure. It's nothing, really..."],["Melissa","Nothing? Hey! Rebecca! We're about to recover our debt! Hello?!"],["Melissa","Sámi's equipment must be amazing—top-tier stuff! If we pawn it, we'll make bank!"],["Melissa","This is a once-in-a-lifetime opportunity! If we miss it... we'll miss it for good!!!"],["","Leaving Melissa behind to vent on her own, Rebecca turns away and tries dialing Alyson's number. After several rings, she inhales deeply, preparing to muster the energy to clean up this mess..."],["Alyson","Melissa, can you hear me?"],["Melissa","Alyson? You finally sent a message. What exactly did you say to them? Our assets are about to..."],["Alyson","Stop interfering with the NDF mission. Retreat immediately. That's an order."],["Melissa","Huh?"],["Alyson","So those old fogeys were talking to you..."],["Rosemary","Actually, I first wanted to talk to you directly, but I've been really tied up lately. And they approached me first..."],["","A hologram sits in front of Alyson. It's the [Madam]."],["","Upon entering the highest conference room at Doll, she found none of the familiar old faces, only Rosemary waiting quietly, as if she had known all along how things would unfold."],["","For some reason, even Alyson feels an inexplicable sense of suffocation when facing this lady alone."],["Rosemary","It seems we now have the chance to clear up some uncertainties..."],["Alyson","If your goal was a conversation, why did you welcome the Doll Group's armed forces into Milkhama without my consent, binding my steps?"],["Rosemary","To establish a cooperative relationship, the higher-ups of the Doll Group decided to support the currently weaker NDF in this manner... I didn't expect them to keep you out of the loop, For that, I'd like to apologize."],["","This is not an apology, just another form of notification. Leaving no room for rebuttal."],["Alyson","Heh... So now you know, I'm just a propped-up figurehead. Even so, are you still willing to sit and talk with me?"],["Rosemary","Why not? After all, who's to say we won't be able to cooperate in the future?"],["","\"The old woman doesn't even deny it?\" Alyson thinks viciously."],["Alyson","I'm afraid I must dampen your optimism. The cooperation between the UNCS and Doll in the ST trade—no, I should say, the economy of Milkhama—may soon become century's biggest punchline."],["Rosemary","You have doubts? Do share."],["Alyson","I can tell you, it's not just this current deal—the entire ST market on this island is a disaster waiting to happen."],["Alyson","Within a year, when the floating interest rate takes effect, the default rate on ST loans will be sent soaring. The whole thing's going down in flames."],["Alyson","If you don't understand these financial terms, let me put it another way: neither of the two forces on this island has done their job properly."],["Alyson","You let the ST factories recklessly develop and produce STs, then dump them on desperate individuals who have no ability to repay... Do you understand? A merc could probably show up with a dog as collateral and still walk away with a new ST."],["Alyson","Soon, when the default rate climbs to 14%, all bonds will become worthless, and everyone on Milkhama will start panic-selling, only to find it's worth no more than an <yellow>empty check</yellow>..."],["Rosemary","Alyson, you're quite perceptive."],["Alyson","...Huh?"],["","The sudden compliment leaves Alyson a bit stunned, while Rosemary's expression remains unchanged in the face of the chaos she has depicted."],["Rosemary","Your elders have also asked me similar questions... So, if it were you, what would you do?"],["Alyson","So... solutions? First, you need to raise the interest rates across Milkhama, regulate the ST market, and then implement appropriate fiscal interventions... No..."],["","Suddenly asked such a question, Alyson is at a loss. She gives some standard answers that any financial worker might say, and then denies herself."],["Alyson","Those old guys... have noticed it too..."],["Rosemary","That's right, they once had the same troubles as you and gave the same answers I imagined."],["Alyson","..."],["Alyson","So their advice is..."],["","Alyson's voice shrinks, as if speaking louder would make everything come true."],["","The last time this topic came up was with those guys from GKD Parcel Service, but she knew, even then, that such a future was out of the question."],["","Back then, there were still all kinds of limits, and Blair's fanciful hopes were bound to fail. It just made her sound like some spoiled rich girl mouthing off for kicks."],["","But now it's different. Money's eating away at those so-called limits, and she knows exactly what people will do when there's profit on the line."],["","So, the answer is..."],["Alyson","..."],["","Alyson doesn't speak the answer. A sense of helplessness stifles her. She feels suffocated."],["","In the past two days, she has been running around to deny that answer, gathering clues, attempting to prevent the upper echelons of Doll from getting involved. But now, as she speaks it out, she realizes the truth is unavoidable."],["","There is no commercial game here, only the inevitability of fate."],["Alyson","You need an opportunity to cash in on this empty promise, allowing those produced STs to be put to use. Then, a continuous flow of funds will pour in again, filling the gap left by the burst bubble... No, the market will grow exponentially..."],["Rosemary","That is the simplest method, and one that no one can avoid. For this reason, I'm deploying troops from the homeland to Milkhama."],["","Noticing Alyson's somewhat suspicious look, Rosemary smiles and explains the intricacies."],["Rosemary","I'm not afraid of you leaking information. The more people know about this, the more likely we can avoid an outcome no one wants to see."],["Rosemary","That's what deterrence is all about."],["Alyson","...You must have sweetened the deal for those old guys. Otherwise I doubt they'd choose to personally get involved in this mess."],["Rosemary","Are you referring to the restrictions imposed on you?"],["Alyson","Haha... It's certainly attractive to them, but it's not enough."],["Rosemary","The UNCS Academy of Science and Engineering will share some of its research achievements with Doll Industries, working together to explore new heights in ST R&D... This is the new report to be published tomorrow."],["Alyson","As expected, they've been coveting that cutting-edge technology for a long time... Apart from Obsidian, it's something that companies like us just can't match."],["Rosemary","Speaking of which, my subordinates have sent some news. It seems that there is a dispute with the Doll Group's mercenaries. Something to do with the right to \"Ursprung\" ST parts originally belonging to the designer Harrison..."],["Rosemary","I wonder—would you mind mediating?"],["","Half a day later, late at night...The Dr. Royal Hotel, Rayneburg"],["Rebecca","Melissa, have you tried this? It makes the beef jerky I used to eat seem like tree bark."],["Melissa","Where is it, where is it? Wait a minute, Rebecca, why are you using their napkins? What if they charge us?"],["Melissa","No, I almost forgot, Alyson is covering this meal... So... don't mind if I do..."],["","In the top-floor restaurant of the most luxurious hotel in Rayneburg, Melissa and Rebecca are enjoying a feast beyond their wildest dreams while overlooking the city's night view."],["","Under Alyson's instructions, the two stopped obstructing Marcus's troops and returned to Rayneburg, where they met at a hotel under her name."],["Alyson","Er, whoa there... should I have the kitchen serve the dishes even faster?"],["Melissa","No... No need. Just let me rest a bit. I still have room..."],["","Melissa wipes the food residue from the corner of her mouth with a napkin, lets out a satisfied burp, and looks at Alyson, who is absentmindedly observing the cityscape in the distance."],["Melissa","Because I'm a bit worried, I'll ask again, have all those securities in my hand really been dealt with?"],["Alyson","Well... it's more or less like that. Although there was some loss, you can just cover it with the reward from this task. Just pretend nothing happened."],["Melissa","Turns out there wasn't much to worry about. Sometimes, nothing beats a false alarm..."],["Alyson","I've arranged rooms for you here. I'll have someone take you there when you've finished eating. The facilities here are quite complete, so make sure you get a good rest over the next few days."],["Melissa","Miss Alyson..."],["Alyson","I know what you're going to ask. Don't worry, it's all paid for."],["Melissa","No, I'd love to have a little break, but can we first go and service the STs?"],["Alyson","..."],["","At times like this, no answer is itself an answer."],["Rebecca","Isn't it a bit strange? She used to gather us at that factory first. When have we ever gone straight to a champagne celebration without reporting the mission?"],["Alyson","So you noticed it too? Yet you still came..."],["Rebecca","Because Melissa is the type who would jump into a trap even if she's seen it..."],["Melissa","Don't say anything... How could I turn down a request from you?"],["","Alyson's calm gaze wavers slightly as she turns her head to look at Melissa and the others. Initially, they had to follow her orders due to debt, but now the situation seems to have changed."],["Melissa","It seems there's indeed trouble on the horizon. Is there anything we can do?"],["Alyson","Heh... something you can do, you say..."],["","That's like asking how to stop humanity from destroying itself."],["Alyson","Honestly, there's not much we can do right now. We can only place our hopes on others."],["Melissa","Are those people ones Alyson can trust?"],["Alyson","I trust them as I trust you."],["Melissa","Alright then... I trust you. We'll follow your plan and lounge about like idiots for the next few days."],["Melissa","By the way, will you be counting our work hours during this time? We won't have our pay docked because of the team-building activities, right?"]]};
